// Into a fissure from its east mouth (24 m down): over the rubble lying on the iron bridge stub and down onto
// the broken timber bridge across the drop. Known layout blockers (sites.rs; see REFINE-movement.md): the
// rubble on the iron stub leaves the gap past the bridges about a cell narrower than the mole, so the lower
// 16 m (the 32 m bridge and the floor) can't be reached without digging; the upper rope hangs under the 8 m
// bridge it's tied to, so it can't be reached from the west mouth; and the ledges overhang the walls, so
// there's no climbing from the east mouth up to the west one.
map
